# ---------------- Animation.events (Task 33 Part E) ----------------
# The animation-depth kit in one sheet: a hit timed by the clip itself, an authored marker as the
# alternative to that percent, a shooting layer over a walk, live speed and the root-motion switch.
# Every word here is shipped (Task 33 Parts A-D), so this file is also the acceptance sheet for
# Task 33's play-check list in Tasks_2.md.
#
# SETUP (editor):
#   1. Player: an AnimatedModel with clips named Attack, Shoot, Aim and Walk (any skeleton; the
#      bridge matches clip names loosely and warns once per unknown name).
#   2. For `hits "impact"`: a Marker Anim Event on Attack's Animation Event track, named impact.
#      Flax keeps a clip's event list editor-side, so a clip without one never fires that trigger —
#      the `reaches 60%` block below is the fallback, and the two are alternatives: keep one.
#   3. For the upper-body layer: Task 33 Part C's authored base Anim Graph (a Blend With Mask whose
#      Pose B is an Animation Slot named UpperBody) plus a SkeletonMask with the spine and arms
#      enabled and the hips, root, legs and feet disabled. Without that graph the layer warns and
#      does nothing, so the legs keep walking either way.
#   4. For root motion: an authored base graph with root motion enabled and a clip imported with
#      root motion. On the bridge's own single-clip graphs the word warns and ignores it.
#
# Keys: Left Mouse attacks, Right Mouse fires the layered shot, Left Shift jogs the animation.

# --- a hit timed by the clip, not a guessed wait ---
when Left Mouse is pressed
  play anim "Attack"

when anim "Attack" starts
  set my ComboWindow to 1

when anim "Attack" reaches 60%
  damage area around me by my Damage for radius 180
  play sound "swing"

when anim "Attack" reaches 100%
  set my ComboWindow to 0

# --- the marker form: drop the 60% block above and author `impact` on the clip instead ---
when anim "Attack" hits "impact"
  set my ImpactFromMarker to 1

# --- shooting while walking: the legs keep the locomotion clip ---
when Right Mouse is pressed
  play anim "Shoot" upper body

when anim "Shoot" ends
  stop anim upper body

# --- live speed, and letting the clip move the actor ---
when Left Shift is held
  set anim speed to 1.8

when Left Shift is released
  set anim speed to 1

when me appears
  loop anim "Walk"
  set root motion on
